1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,475
Ransomware locks your files and demands money for the key. Hospitals, schools and shops have all been hit.

2
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:19,370
Backups are the seatbelt of computing: boring, until the day they save you. Keep three copies, on two kinds of storage, with one offline.

3
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:29,020
Use separate admin accounts. Do daily work with a normal account, like keeping the master key in the safe.

4
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:36,670
Remove access the day someone leaves, and get alerts for new sign-ins and new forwarding rules.

5
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:45,570
A backup you have never restored is a hope, not a backup. Test restoring every few months.

6
00:00:46,270 --> 00:00:53,620
Protect email above all, because it can reset every other password. Two-step sign-in everywhere.

